                        <p class="mt-5 text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-white/90 leading-snug">Evidence the other side can check without you.</p>
                        <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-white/70 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">A signed ledger and exports an auditor can take away.</p>
                        <p class="mt-8 text-lg text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
                            Your model provider's log lives on their infrastructure, signed with their keys, read through their console. The suspect cannot write the police report. KYDE's record is captured at the boundary before anything reaches a provider and hash-chained, so altering one link breaks every link after it. <span class="text-white/35">The ledger and the exports run today; signing each entry with your own keys is an Enterprise capability.</span>
                        </p>
